WEBVTT

00:05.970 --> 00:08.770
It's all going according to script.

00:09.490 --> 00:13.280
I tried to create the ultimate game.

00:13.700 --> 00:16.820
One that copies nothing, 
that nobody can copy.

00:16.820 --> 00:19.200
I embody that originality.

00:19.200 --> 00:22.780
I am the true creator!

00:23.360 --> 00:27.280
But with the creator of this 
world standing before you,

00:27.280 --> 00:29.130
I say it is all fiction.

00:29.550 --> 00:33.280
You are all nothing but simple NPCs,

00:33.280 --> 00:35.880
living and dying 
in the roles you were given.

00:36.530 --> 00:39.470
But I alone am different!

00:39.470 --> 00:44.100
I was chosen to be 
the designer of a new world!

00:44.100 --> 00:48.940
And to be your playable character.

00:49.770 --> 00:51.690
How does my script look now?

00:51.980 --> 00:53.950
Are you enjoying it,

00:54.800 --> 00:55.790
Origin?

00:56.440 --> 00:59.450
Well, will it appear soon?

01:00.080 --> 01:03.270
The final flag.

01:47.960 --> 01:51.400
Magical Destroyers.

01:56.050 --> 02:02.180
<b>What You Like, as Much as You Like</b>

02:02.300 --> 02:05.090
Anarchy-chan! Blue-chan! Pink-chan!

02:05.090 --> 02:07.540
It's me! It's Otaku Hero!

02:07.540 --> 02:08.850
Don't you recognize me?

02:10.380 --> 02:11.810
Anarchy-chan!

02:30.200 --> 02:33.200
Shobon!

02:36.200 --> 02:40.470
Yeah!

02:36.200 --> 02:40.470
We did it!

02:36.200 --> 02:40.470
All right!

02:51.500 --> 02:52.360
Yes!

02:52.360 --> 02:54.660
The enemy has totally 
lost their will to fight!

02:54.660 --> 02:55.820
Awesome!

02:55.820 --> 02:57.610
We actually did it!

02:57.610 --> 03:00.010
The otaku have won!

03:00.010 --> 03:01.720
Yeah! Oh, that's right.

03:01.720 --> 03:02.740
We were gonna...

03:02.740 --> 03:03.990
Raise the flag!

03:03.990 --> 03:07.490
Plant it up there and 
we'll celebrate our victory!

03:07.490 --> 03:08.840
All right!

03:08.840 --> 03:11.950
Wait, hold on! Otaku Hero still has it!

03:11.950 --> 03:14.790
Yeah, he's got to be the one to end this.

03:15.000 --> 03:16.710
What is Otaku Hero's position?

03:16.710 --> 03:19.500
I heard he was heading to Akiba, I say.

03:19.500 --> 03:20.460
Akiba?

03:20.460 --> 03:22.060
Geez, what bad timing!

03:22.060 --> 03:24.270
<i>Guys! Guys!</i>

03:24.270 --> 03:25.880
Guys! Can you hear me?

03:25.880 --> 03:28.260
Nick and Old Leader here.

03:28.260 --> 03:28.880
We're both—

03:28.880 --> 03:32.640
<i>HQ, our troops have successfully 
taken control of the enemy base!</i>

03:32.640 --> 03:33.570
Whoa!

03:33.570 --> 03:34.520
Seriously?

03:34.520 --> 03:35.530
Yeah!

03:35.530 --> 03:37.800
It's going viral across the country!

03:37.800 --> 03:39.600
<i>Nice job, guys!</i>

03:39.600 --> 03:41.740
<i>But we've still got a problem!</i>

03:42.150 --> 03:45.560
<i>This time you really gotta withdraw 
and come back to Akiba!</i>

03:45.560 --> 03:46.910
What?

03:45.560 --> 03:46.910
Huh? Why?

03:46.910 --> 03:48.290
<i>Why though?</i>

03:48.290 --> 03:50.930
Anarchy-chan and the girls have gone crazy,

03:52.160 --> 03:54.480
and Shobon is in Akiba!

03:56.520 --> 03:59.000
Hey. It's been a while.

03:59.000 --> 04:00.040
Screw you!

04:00.040 --> 04:03.530
A while back, I said something to you.

04:03.530 --> 04:08.800
"The next time we meet, who will achieve 
the world they envisioned?" Right?

04:09.950 --> 04:12.810
What have you done 
to Anarchy-chan and the girls?!

04:12.810 --> 04:16.490
Oh, but you already know the answer to that.

04:18.070 --> 04:19.650
You won't admit it.

04:19.660 --> 04:22.820
You think it's fake, made up, phony.

04:22.820 --> 04:25.800
Some kind of trap. 
Is that what you want to believe?

04:22.820 --> 04:28.330
Anarchy Roars

04:22.820 --> 04:28.330
Transforms into Destroyer

04:22.820 --> 04:28.330
Blue also transforms into Destroyer
Blue wields a scythe
with a mean look in her eyes

04:22.820 --> 04:28.330
Pink transforms into Destroyer,
waves her cloak, and poses

04:25.800 --> 04:27.640
But it's pointless.

04:27.640 --> 04:32.210
And you already realize that it's pointless.

04:28.330 --> 04:32.200
The magical girls
transform into Destroyers
and betray him

04:32.210 --> 04:33.250
Shut up!

04:33.390 --> 04:36.300
I had you all in the palm of my hand.

04:36.300 --> 04:38.710
Of course, with one exception.

04:38.980 --> 04:40.350
Kyotaro?

04:41.230 --> 04:42.840
Are you getting it now?

04:42.840 --> 04:44.620
You sure are a sharp one.

04:44.620 --> 04:48.720
There was nothing written 
about Kyotaro in the notebook!

04:45.760 --> 04:46.970
silhouettes of
Four Heavenly
Kings on top
of building

04:45.760 --> 04:46.970
otaku hiding

04:45.760 --> 04:46.970
Explosion

04:45.760 --> 04:46.970
Smoke clears
and

04:46.970 --> 04:49.480
Chogo-shi typing
notes on tape

04:46.970 --> 04:49.480
Cardboard box
by showcase has

04:46.970 --> 04:49.480
figurines thrown away with
empty cup noodle containers

04:48.720 --> 04:50.660
That's exactly right!

04:50.660 --> 04:53.060
And for good reason, too.

04:53.060 --> 04:57.250
This is the game's one and only player,

04:57.250 --> 04:59.950
just here to enjoy the whole thing.

04:59.950 --> 05:03.130
Watching over this new world from above,

05:03.130 --> 05:06.320
existing everywhere and nowhere at once.

05:15.330 --> 05:18.860
That is the nature of Origin's being.

05:29.130 --> 05:30.350
Origin...

05:31.200 --> 05:35.970
Huh. Kyotaro-kun, 
so that was your true identity?

05:35.970 --> 05:37.800
You were so cute.

05:37.800 --> 05:40.080
I had no idea where you came from,

05:40.080 --> 05:41.980
but this makes everything hunky-dory!

05:42.330 --> 05:43.940
The hell it does.

05:44.730 --> 05:48.760
Game? Player? Enjoy this?

05:48.760 --> 05:51.960
Nothing you just said makes any sense!

05:52.710 --> 05:55.880
I don't know what you have against otaku,

05:55.880 --> 05:58.480
but you want to make me 
play along with this?

05:58.480 --> 06:01.770
With this game or whatever?

06:02.210 --> 06:05.460
That's stupid as shit!

06:06.800 --> 06:08.040
P-Pink-cha—

06:11.510 --> 06:15.720
Screw your game! Screw your script!

06:16.310 --> 06:17.810
B-Blue-cha—

06:20.300 --> 06:23.860
Screw your new world!

06:25.920 --> 06:30.610
Why? Why do you hate otaku?

06:31.910 --> 06:33.260
Anarchy-chan?

06:46.480 --> 06:48.590
Otaku Hero...

06:52.650 --> 06:57.600
I want to like what 
I like as much as I like.

06:59.000 --> 07:02.360
What's... What's wrong with that?

07:03.800 --> 07:06.990
You really are essential to this game.

07:06.990 --> 07:10.570
Don't you have something, 
anything that you like?

07:12.600 --> 07:16.740
Yeah, I just love creating worlds!

07:16.740 --> 07:20.880
I put my entire being into making this game,

07:20.880 --> 07:23.470
to reject the otaku who tried to reject me.

07:23.470 --> 07:25.470
To eradicate them!

07:25.470 --> 07:28.100
Yeah, I finally get it.

07:28.610 --> 07:30.300
You're a piece of shit!

07:34.570 --> 07:38.230
Otaku all have something. 
Something they like.

07:38.930 --> 07:42.520
Something that they can't live without.

07:43.020 --> 07:45.610
No matter who tries to reject them,

07:46.920 --> 07:49.230
no matter how much they try to reject them,

07:50.600 --> 07:52.860
they can't stop being who they are!

07:54.790 --> 07:58.420
I like anime.

07:58.980 --> 08:00.540
I like manga.

08:00.870 --> 08:04.350
I like models. I like music!

08:04.350 --> 08:09.810
The others like idols and tokusatsu 
and figures and cosplay and military stuff,

08:09.810 --> 08:12.960
and model trains and adult 
dojinshi! They love them!

08:12.960 --> 08:14.780
And why?

08:14.780 --> 08:17.880
Because they can feel the spirit 
of the people who created them!

08:17.880 --> 08:22.150
They all share the urge to like—
to really like something!

08:22.150 --> 08:24.170
But this game is different!

08:24.950 --> 08:26.280
Why won't you go down?

08:26.280 --> 08:30.310
This game is made from an urge to hate!

08:30.310 --> 08:32.560
I'm not okay with that.

08:32.770 --> 08:38.290
You think we'll let something like 
that take away what we like?!

08:38.290 --> 08:39.130
He's right!

08:39.130 --> 08:40.290
He's exactly right!

08:40.290 --> 08:40.980
Yeah!

08:40.980 --> 08:41.650
Don't let him win!

08:41.650 --> 08:42.420
Keep fighting!

08:42.420 --> 08:43.270
Get him!

08:43.270 --> 08:44.500
Otaku Hero!

08:44.500 --> 08:45.550
I say!

08:45.550 --> 08:49.490
Now give us back our world!

08:49.850 --> 08:54.000
Don't mess with otaku!

09:16.830 --> 09:19.490
What happened?

09:16.830 --> 09:19.490
What the...?

09:29.360 --> 09:31.980
I'm the designer of this world.

09:31.980 --> 09:35.680
A creator exists outside of his creation.

09:35.680 --> 09:38.870
Why would you expect this 
to be my real body?

09:38.870 --> 09:41.680
You don't have a... real body?

09:41.680 --> 09:42.520
No.

09:42.880 --> 09:44.520
You can't beat me.

09:42.880 --> 09:44.520
I can't beat you.

09:44.520 --> 09:47.110
I do thank you, Otaku Hero.

09:47.110 --> 09:49.900
You raised the magical girls for me.

09:50.130 --> 09:53.810
The girls fought against 
their complementary colors,

09:53.810 --> 09:57.650
and bathed in that blood, 
returned to their original forms.

09:58.440 --> 10:03.390
You certainly were a hero, 
because you were the only one in this world

10:03.390 --> 10:06.530
who wasn't colored by somebody else.

10:06.780 --> 10:09.520
You're the icon that symbolizes this game.

10:09.520 --> 10:12.980
You're both the hero and the final boss!

10:12.980 --> 10:16.050
Well? Isn't that a fantastic idea?

10:16.050 --> 10:21.040
By killing you, the world will 
finally be painted all one color,

10:21.040 --> 10:24.120
bringing forth a new order 
and a world with no otaku!

10:24.770 --> 10:25.820
Origin.

10:25.820 --> 10:26.560
Huh?

10:26.760 --> 10:27.930
It's the end.

10:29.220 --> 10:31.550
Magical Destroyers.

10:41.930 --> 10:43.200
Don't do it!

10:43.200 --> 10:44.330
Please stop!

10:44.330 --> 10:46.750
Don't! Stop!

10:46.750 --> 10:47.720
Please!

10:47.720 --> 10:48.960
Don't do it!

10:48.960 --> 10:52.710
Please don't kill Otaku Hero!

10:55.010 --> 10:57.760
What's wrong? Hurry up and kill him.

11:08.100 --> 11:10.480
Wh-What's this? It can't be...

11:23.120 --> 11:24.520
Ta-da!

11:25.560 --> 11:26.870
Well?

11:27.920 --> 11:30.230
Christmas Eve?

11:32.240 --> 11:33.760
Yeah! It looks great on you! {same as ep 6 17:54~}

11:33.760 --> 11:35.860
What? Are you being serious?

11:35.860 --> 11:36.500
Huh?

11:38.760 --> 11:40.390
This isn't cute at all!

11:40.610 --> 11:44.800
Even ignoring the low quality of the
needlework, this is just not...

11:44.800 --> 11:47.140
Gobo-go gobo!

11:45.400 --> 11:47.140
"Design sense: zero!"

11:49.040 --> 11:50.660
What a tough crowd.

11:50.660 --> 11:51.460
Geez!

11:51.460 --> 11:54.780
This is the first Christmas 
present I've ever gotten,

11:54.780 --> 11:58.800
and it's stupid and ugly,
and obviously your fetish!

11:59.950 --> 12:03.280
We really can't... 
count on you for anything.

12:03.600 --> 12:05.600
You're always daydreaming.

12:05.600 --> 12:08.360
You're kind of nice, 
but you're such a chicken.

12:09.140 --> 12:11.800
You're just a stupid otaku.

12:11.800 --> 12:13.170
Gobo...

12:14.000 --> 12:16.300
But you still...

12:17.570 --> 12:19.290
You still...

12:20.040 --> 12:23.300
...mean everything to us.

12:25.730 --> 12:26.800
Thanks.

12:27.520 --> 12:27.960
But I—

12:27.960 --> 12:29.370
Don't say it!

12:39.170 --> 12:41.210
It really is time to say goodbye.

12:42.290 --> 12:45.130
I wish I could stay with you all,

12:45.450 --> 12:47.500
but something is waiting for me,

12:47.500 --> 12:49.830
and it's more important 
than my own feelings.

12:50.190 --> 12:52.040
I need to light the fire of revolution.

12:52.320 --> 12:56.840
And then change this twisted world back.

12:56.840 --> 12:58.230
Gobo-bo!

12:57.320 --> 12:59.210
Yeah, but do it with us!

12:59.210 --> 13:00.850
I can't do that.

13:01.210 --> 13:06.480
I want you all to live 
and remember what we tried to do.

13:08.400 --> 13:11.210
Don't say things like that!

13:11.480 --> 13:16.410
After this, no matter what happens, 
no matter what shape it takes,

13:16.410 --> 13:19.850
my otaku soul will live on.

13:19.850 --> 13:21.360
I'm begging you!

13:21.360 --> 13:23.120
It's okay! I'm sure of it!

13:23.120 --> 13:25.320
I promise we'll meet again!

13:27.490 --> 13:28.910
Gobo bobo!

13:28.910 --> 13:30.910
No! Don't go away!

13:30.910 --> 13:32.670
Otaku Hero!

13:35.960 --> 13:40.000
<i>If I round up, I'm basically 30.</i>

13:36.920 --> 13:41.550
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

13:40.640 --> 13:43.930
<i>I wish I could use magic 
just for this night.</i>

13:50.180 --> 13:51.560
Merry Christmas.

14:27.840 --> 14:31.110
My precious notebook got dirty.

14:37.380 --> 14:40.350
Hey, Origin! Don't peek!

14:40.350 --> 14:43.920
We've only finished phase one. 
There's more to do!

14:52.530 --> 14:54.780
Protect Otaku

14:59.120 --> 15:01.500
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

15:09.380 --> 15:12.960
Shobon had us all in the palm of his hand.

15:12.960 --> 15:15.260
He was just playing with us.

15:15.520 --> 15:17.260
All of our battles...

15:17.260 --> 15:18.440
And our victories...

15:18.440 --> 15:20.520
Taking the Diet building...

15:20.690 --> 15:23.300
were just a god's way of killing time.

15:23.300 --> 15:25.520
They were toying with us the whole time.

15:25.710 --> 15:27.740
Otaku Hero!

15:30.740 --> 15:33.740
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

15:56.120 --> 15:58.640
<i>Remaining Revolutionary 
Army members located.</i>

15:58.640 --> 16:00.010
<i>Apprehend them immediately.</i>

16:00.010 --> 16:03.030
<i>They're collecting artifacts 
at building ruins.</i>

16:03.480 --> 16:07.490
<i>All units, surround them 
and wait for the order to move in.</i>

16:09.990 --> 16:10.780
Okay!

16:10.780 --> 16:12.600
Come on, you've gotten enough.

16:12.600 --> 16:15.170
Hold on. Just one last thing.

16:16.210 --> 16:17.910
That's plenty. Let's go.

16:21.100 --> 16:22.420
It's SSC!

16:22.420 --> 16:24.160
Are we done for?

16:24.480 --> 16:26.850
Huh? Anarchy-chan?

16:27.920 --> 16:29.160
Blue-chan!

16:29.160 --> 16:30.180
And Pink-chan!

16:30.180 --> 16:31.520
I don't get it.

16:31.520 --> 16:33.650
We fought together

16:33.650 --> 16:36.300
to win back freedom for otaku!

16:36.300 --> 16:38.560
Didn't you vow to defeat Shobon?

16:38.560 --> 16:39.870
And now this? Why?

16:39.870 --> 16:41.610
Silence, vermin.

16:51.380 --> 16:54.000
<i>Targets apprehended. Returning to base.</i>

16:59.050 --> 17:04.080
<i>In December of 2011, 
everything suddenly ended.</i>

17:04.080 --> 17:08.220
<i>With the Magical Destroyers now awakened, 
the world moved into "Phase 2"</i>

17:08.220 --> 17:11.870
<i>and fell under the control 
of Shobon and the girls.</i>

17:12.250 --> 17:15.210
<i>Following the death of their leader, 
the Otaku Revolutionary Army crumbled</i>

17:15.210 --> 17:16.510
<i>and its members scattered.</i>

17:17.010 --> 17:19.510
<b>SSC Era Year 2</b>

17:17.630 --> 17:19.520
<i>Now two years have passed.</i>

17:19.520 --> 17:23.920
<i>The Magical Destroyers have 
become SSC's top officers</i>

17:23.920 --> 17:26.020
<i>and maintain order in the world.</i>

17:26.020 --> 17:31.020
2 Years Since His Death

17:26.020 --> 17:31.020
SSC Plans Ceremony to Celebrate Extermination of Insurrectionist Arm

17:26.350 --> 17:30.560
<i>Many otaku witnessed the death 
of the Revolutionary Army leader.</i>

17:30.560 --> 17:33.300
<i>SSC also spread news of his death.</i>

17:31.020 --> 17:35.240
<b>Cabinet Meeting, Ceremony Planned to Commemorate Extermination of Otaku
"Otaku Hero did in fact die"
--SSC University Honorary Professor Shobon's Declaration
A Great Shock to the Otaku World
Do Otaku Have a Future??
SSC Newspaper Morning Edition Now On Sale</b>

17:32.030 --> 17:35.700
<b>Did Otaku Hero survive?
A reporter dug up the grave to reveal the truth.
Weekly SSC</b>

17:34.120 --> 17:35.200
<i>Regardless of that,</i>

17:36.850 --> 17:39.030
<i>rumors and urban legends circulated,</i>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b>huh? Uh</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b>uh... no</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b> nah he's alive I saw him!</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b>were you an otaku?</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b> but they reported that
Otaku Hero died</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b>good bye</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:39.820
<b>Isikawa blocked Bayashi</b>

17:39.030 --> 17:40.650
<i>saying he was still alive.</i>

17:41.540 --> 17:48.040
<i>This proved that a wish for it to 
be true still smoldered in people's hearts.</i>

17:51.010 --> 17:53.880
<i>In order to extinguish 
that hope, however small,</i>

17:53.880 --> 17:59.850
<i>SSC and the Magical Destroyers 
have continued to hunt otaku.</i>

18:03.390 --> 18:05.310
Second Anniversary of the Extermination of the Insurrectionist Army

18:05.310 --> 18:08.100
Second Anniversary of the Extermination of the Insurrectionist Army

18:15.200 --> 18:18.510
We of SSC, leaders of the new world order,

18:18.510 --> 18:22.870
sent that evil disrupter of public morals, 
Otaku Hero, to his grave!

18:23.160 --> 18:27.950
The magical girls we are so very proud of

18:27.950 --> 18:32.380
brought true peace 
to this country on this very spot.

18:34.200 --> 18:35.630
However!

18:36.240 --> 18:40.960
That evil ideology still clings 
on in different parts of Japan.

18:40.960 --> 18:42.140
Behold!

18:42.140 --> 18:44.910
In two years, in only two years,

18:44.910 --> 18:47.140
we have collected this 
massive mountain of trash!

18:47.400 --> 18:51.400
This means that our battle is far from over.

18:51.400 --> 18:57.150
This shows how much danger, 
how much poison still remains in our nation.

18:57.150 --> 19:01.530
Until we completely annihilate 
their dangerous ideology,

19:01.530 --> 19:02.960
we will continue fighting!

19:02.960 --> 19:06.730
Yeah!

19:06.730 --> 19:07.840
Did you hear?

19:07.840 --> 19:08.660
About what?

19:08.800 --> 19:10.870
Apparently, he's still alive.

19:10.870 --> 19:12.170
No way!

19:12.170 --> 19:14.040
They say they haven't found it yet.

19:14.040 --> 19:15.540
The helmet?

19:30.060 --> 19:31.050
Burn it all!

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
Crowd at the
ceremony goes wild

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
people clap and yell
and get excited

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
Cofficers surround
the mountain of merch

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
Burn it all!

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
gives the signal

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
Cofficers holding
flamethrowers

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
shoot flames

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
merch pile burns

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
Whoa!

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
crowd goes wild

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
at top of trash heap,
Otaku Hero's helmet burning

19:39.320 --> 19:41.200
I watch it all happen

19:41.200 --> 19:43.450
At top of trash heap

19:41.200 --> 19:43.450
Otaku Hero's helmet burning

19:49.950 --> 19:50.970
What's that?

19:50.970 --> 19:51.960
An earthquake?

19:54.560 --> 19:55.810
Where did it go?

19:58.460 --> 19:59.970
Run!

19:59.970 --> 20:01.460
Help!

20:02.350 --> 20:04.140
Th-This is...

20:04.720 --> 20:05.970
The End

20:04.920 --> 20:05.960
What?!

20:05.960 --> 20:08.090
This isn't in the script!

20:10.640 --> 20:13.310
Yeah!

20:13.310 --> 20:15.420
Damn them!

20:16.130 --> 20:17.230
What?!

20:17.560 --> 20:21.340
It ca— It can't... It can't be!

20:21.340 --> 20:22.860
It's impossible!

20:35.880 --> 20:37.120
You punk.

20:38.720 --> 20:41.000
Merry Christmas, assholes!

20:41.000 --> 20:41.970
Who is that?!

20:41.970 --> 20:44.230
I'm Otaku Hero the Second.

20:44.230 --> 20:45.720
We'll take the First's ideals

20:45.720 --> 20:49.720
and continue on 
as the True Otaku Revolutionary Army!

20:50.210 --> 20:52.790
A second-generation Otaku Hero?

20:52.790 --> 20:53.980
Shobon!

20:53.980 --> 20:56.680
The flames of revolution have risen again!

20:56.680 --> 21:00.100
We'll burn you with 
the fire of passion in our hearts!

21:00.610 --> 21:02.860
If you get in our way, you'll be sorry,

21:02.860 --> 21:04.650
Magical Destroyers!

21:22.160 --> 21:27.420
It's okay! I promise we'll meet again!

21:32.800 --> 21:35.230
Yeah, come and get it!

21:39.280 --> 21:41.360
This isn't right! It's not in the script!

21:41.360 --> 21:43.200
Not in the script!

21:43.200 --> 21:46.440
This can't be right!

21:53.320 --> 21:54.590
Gobo gobo.

21:54.590 --> 21:57.580
Think you got what it takes, bro?

21:57.580 --> 22:00.000
We'll take you on.

22:00.490 --> 22:05.430
What you like, as much as you like!
